cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or data, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Who Gets the Shade? Ranking New York Neighborhoods for Tree Planting"
version: "1.0.0"
authors:
  - family-names: "Fernandez"
    given-names: "Jhoven"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0000-1526-4744"
abstract: >-
  Working paper and reproducible code. Using public data for New York City's
  42 UHF neighborhoods, the study tests whether the rule a city uses to rank
  neighborhoods for tree planting changes who benefits, and whether a
  heat-illness model transfers across boroughs. Methods include Moran's I and
  LISA, spatial lag and error models, leave-one-borough-out cross-validation
  and 5,000 random ranking weightings. Not yet peer reviewed.
repository-code: "https://github.com/jhovenf98/who-gets-the-shade"
url: "https://jhovenf98.github.io/geoai-for-cities/explore/shade.html"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - urban heat
  - tree canopy
  - environmental justice
  - spatial analysis
  - New York City
